%>pretty irrelevant; it has been a long time since I used an
%>unmodified article style.
%>
%>Michael Barr
%>

True! Almost every one of my documents to be printed on A4 starts with
\documentstyle[...,A4,...]...
where A4.sty is

\oddsidemargin\z@
\evensidemargin\z@
\topmargin\z@
\advance\topmargin-3\baselineskip
\headheight\baselineskip
\headsep2\baselineskip
\textwidth210mm \advance\textwidth -2in
\textheight297mm \advance\textheight-2in
\footskip2\baselineskip
\columnseprule0.1pt

Either that, or bigA4, giving a .25 inch margin, or fullA4, using the whole
paper area.

And if we want portability, we package the styles with the documents.
Mike

PS I guess someone will write back and tell me that (a) I shouldn't assume
that \z@ will stay constant in LaTeX-3, and (b) A4.sty already exists on CTAN.


